Verify the RANDAO signature inline during block processing.

Upstream ProcessBlockForStateRoot uses ProcessRandaoNoVerify and instead returns
the RANDAO signature in the batch that ProcessBlockNoVerifyAnySig hands back, so
a bad reveal only surfaces after the whole block has been processed. pyspec's
process_randao raises at that point in the sequence, before eth1_data and the
operations, and differential testing compares which failure a client reports.

diff --git a/beacon-chain/core/transition/transition_no_verify_sig.go b/beacon-chain/core/transition/transition_no_verify_sig.go
index 2873301..f4425a6 100644
--- a/beacon-chain/core/transition/transition_no_verify_sig.go
+++ b/beacon-chain/core/transition/transition_no_verify_sig.go
@@ -340,8 +340,8 @@ func ProcessBlockForStateRoot(
 		}
 	}
 
-	randaoReveal := signed.Block().Body().RandaoReveal()
-	state, err = b.ProcessRandaoNoVerify(state, randaoReveal[:])
+	// validate_result = false: Verify RANDAO signature (block signature is skipped in main.go)
+	state, err = b.ProcessRandao(ctx, state, signed)
 	if err != nil {
 		tracing.AnnotateError(span, err)
 		return nil, errors.Wrap(err, "could not verify and process randao")
